+
+
+/* =====================================================================
+   PERFORMANCE PASS  (visuals unchanged; only costs removed)
+
+   1. `transition: --glow` on .ff animated an INHERITED custom property for 0.9s on every card change, so the browser re-resolved styles for the
+      whole subtree (hundreds of nodes, plus every cloned shard) and repainted every gradient that reads var(--glow), on every frame of the
+      scroll. The colour now switches instantly and only the three big colour pools glide, as a plain background-colour transition.
+   2. blur() filters on the aurora / glow layers: their gradients already fade to transparent, so the blur added nothing but a full-layer GPU pass per frame.
+   3. box-shadows on the cards were clipped away by the cards' own clip-path (never visible) but still painted.
+   4. backdrop-filter on the chips, tags and ticker re-blurred what sat behind them every frame.
+   5. rotating a perfectly round, uniformly bordered ring changes nothing on screen.
+   ===================================================================== */
+.ff { transition: none; }
